		{"id":"b4163bde694fe423","type":"text","text":"\n## Security Best Practices\n\n- **UUIDv7** for primary keys.\n- **Argon2id** for password hashing.\n- Store only **hashed refresh tokens**, password reset tokens, API keys, and verification tokens.\n- Support **WebAuthn (passkeys)** and **TOTP MFA**.\n- Track **sessions per device** with the ability to revoke individual or all sessions.\n- Use **soft deletes** (`deleted_at`) for recoverability.\n- Add audit fields (`created_at`, `updated_at`, `last_seen_at`) where appropriate.\n- Enforce unique constraints on usernames, primary emails, OAuth provider IDs, and WebAuthn credential IDs.\n- Separate profile data from authentication and authorization data to minimize the impact of security-sensitive changes.","x":1400,"y":837,"width":932,"height":393},
